# TLS termination and reverse proxy for everything on the box.
#
# ⚠️ Copied here by scripts/oracle-deploy.sh. The previous box's Caddyfile was
# hand-edited over SSH with `.bak` copies beside it as the only history, and
# `docker exec livekit-caddy caddy reload` applied it. Editing the copy on the
# box now means the next deploy overwrites you.

# ── LiveKit signalling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ✅ This is the ONLY hostname whose certificate survives the rebuild. The
# `caddy_data` volume — the ACME account key and the issued certificates — was
# captured off the old box and is restored by the deploy script, so this cert
# carries over intact, valid to 2026-11-27, with no re-issuance and no
# rate-limit exposure.
livekit.spiralclass.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:7880
}

# ── The preview web app ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠️ NEW TO CADDY. There is no certificate for this name in the restored
# volume, so Caddy must obtain one at cutover — and tls-alpn-01 cannot work
# through Cloudflare's proxy (the challenge handshake terminates at the edge),
# so http-01 is the only path.
#
# ⚠️ That makes D-134's invariant govern this hostname too: **"Always Use
# HTTPS" must be OFF and SSL mode must be Full**, or the edge answers the ACME
# challenge with a redirect, issuance fails, and the name has no certificate at
# all. Issue while grey-clouded, verify on the box, then re-proxy.
#
# Preview is deliberately reachable on a real public hostname rather than
# tailnet-only, because it is what a tester uses for UAT — it has to work
# from her machine, not just from the tailnet.
preview.spiralclass.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3001
}

# ── Not configured here, on purpose ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠️ `spiralclass.com` IS NOT HERE, and must not be added. The production web
# app stays on Fly (D-150's second addendum, 2026-09-04) and the apex A record
# keeps pointing there. Adding it here would take a name Caddy cannot serve
# and give it a certificate renewal that fails silently, on the one box whose
# renewals already matter.
#
# `livekit.agendaprofe.com` was dropped on 2026-08-29, completing the D-138
# rename. The old certificate is still in `caddy_data` until it expires
# 2026-10-19, so a fallback before then needs no re-issuance — but it also
# needs the Cloudflare A record re-created and this hostname re-added. Do not
# add it back speculatively; an unused hostname in here is a renewal that can
# fail silently.
#
# Real client IPs: Cloudflare proxies all three names, so Caddy sees edge
# addresses and the app must read `CF-Connecting-IP`. Caddy is NOT configured
# with `trusted_proxies` here, because doing it properly means pinning
# Cloudflare's published ranges and keeping them current — a stale list is
# worse than none. Worth doing deliberately, not as part of a migration.
